  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The passing game – in threes",
  "description": "Split the players into groups of three with one puck per group, spread over the whole rink. Each group passes the puck in turn: A to B, B to C, C to A. Shrink the area if the players can handle it – the groups come closer together and there is more to keep track of.\n\nMove on to free passing within the group, then to 2v1: one in the group chases the puck and the other two pass. Change chaser regularly. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Where should I stand to get the puck?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "When should I pass – before the chaser gets there."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receive with a soft blade and look up for the next one."
    }
  ],
